<title>BELGIUM: EU to discuss voluntary cereals set-aside.</title>
<headline>EU to discuss voluntary cereals set-aside.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The future of voluntary set-aside will be discussed by European Union cereal experts on Thursday, an EU official said.</p>
<p>&quot;The application of voluntary set-aside and its results together with the future prospects will be reviewed by the experts group,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>The group will meet before the weekly meeting of the EU cereals management committee.</p>
<p>The discussion will focus on the way voluntary set-aside has been applied since the 1992 reform of the EU Common Agriculture Policy which introduced compulsory rotational set-aside.</p>
<p>Voluntary set-aside is limited to 50 percent of the arable area eligible for aid.</p>
</text>
